X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:What this proves: a property name in small letters is still recognised, and
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:a value split across two lines (a "fold") is joined back together before it
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:is read. This file writes "private" as "pri" plus a folded "vate". A reader
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:that did not unfold would see the value "pri", not match PUBLIC either, and
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:happen to get the right answer for the wrong reason - so the self-test also
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:checks the title, which is folded in the middle of a word.
